PRIMARY OBJECTIVE
Turn the proven synthetic/ephemeral local SAIMAIL path into one practical persistent local workflow that a real operator can use to:

1. initialize a persistent local workspace;
2. create or load a persistent local identity;
3. address a known local recipient;
4. send one real local SAIMAIL message through existing protocol APIs;
5. list received messages;
6. inspect bounded metadata without opening payload;
7. explicitly open a selected message;
8. preserve state across process exit/restart;
9. handle duplicate/refusal/error states intelligibly.

This is the first practical local product workflow.

It is NOT a GUI wave, external adapter wave, network service, or protocol redesign.

