* persistent workspace requires changing a fundamental envelope/Post Office contract;
* current key APIs cannot persist identity safely enough even for the documented local-alpha threat model;
* recipient addressing requires a broad identity/address-book redesign;
* real send/receive cannot use existing public protocol APIs;
* persistent operation requires bypassing verification/dedup gates;
* clean-wheel execution cannot access the required public surfaces without broad packaging redesign;
* privacy would need to be weakened;
* completing V2-01 requires network/model access;
* a genuine FG-05/FG-06 regression invalidates the foundation;
* unrelated SAIPEN debt blocks lifecycle and requires broad core repair.

On STOP:

* preserve evidence;
* name the exact failing boundary;
* identify the smallest repair;
* do not redesign the whole protocol.

